h('13.1 State-loss and completion limitations');para('The benchmark runner assigns its state-loss percentages and completion flags directly in code. It does not compare application checkpoints, output hashes, durable writes or completed work. Consequently, the reported 0% state-loss value cannot be presented as a measured integrity guarantee.')
h('13.2 ML evidence boundary');para('The README reports normal-telemetry flag rates of 100% for an original model and 2.6% for a candidate, alongside missed synthetic stress scenarios. The underlying dataset and trained artifacts are not present in this checkout. These reported values are not independently reproduced here and do not establish precision, recall or F1. Shadow ML does not decide enforcement.')
page('Review III: synthetic comparison');h('14. Synthetic Recovery-Policy Evaluation');para('The deterministic model sets observed CPU to min(demand, duty). A recovered workload has demand sampled between 0.08 and 0.20 cores; a still-demanding workload is sampled between 0.80 and 1.00. Protected latency is constructed with small seeded noise. Repeated within-window latency values are not independent request measurements.')
data=json.loads((ROOT/'research/recovery_probe/results/synthetic-comparison.json').read_text())
table(['Constructed scenario','Trials','Legacy relaxes','Probe relaxes'],[[r['scenario'],r['trials'],r['legacy_relaxations'],r['probe_relaxations']] for r in data['summary']],[220,60,114,114])
para('The legacy policy receives its ordinary CPU telemetry. The probe receives additional controlled-release and protected-service observations. This compares complete policies with different inputs, not equal-information algorithms. Drift and load-change cases are treated as inconclusive; rejecting them is not proof that their processes are faulty.')
h('14.1 Ablation');para('Removing the normalized-demand check permits relaxation in 100 of 100 hidden-demand cases in this constructed model. The ablation supports the role of that gate under the model, but it does not demonstrate field accuracy or an independently discovered physical effect.')
h('14.2 Reproducibility');para('Results and raw trials are retained in research/recovery_probe/results/synthetic-comparison.json. The simulation uses seeds 0-99 for each scenario. No invented live latency, CPU savings or recovery-time figures are added.')
page('Review III: comparison');h('15. Comparison with Existing Systems');table(['Approach','Established behavior','ARQ boundary'],[['cpulimit','Signal-based CPU restriction.','No novelty claim for SIGSTOP/SIGCONT.'],['Linux cgroup v2','Kernel CPU/memory/I/O resource controls.','ARQ signal pulsing is not equivalent to a cgroup sandbox.'],['CPI2 [10]','Detect interference and throttle likely offenders.','Adaptive throttling of suspected offenders is known.'],['Heracles / PARTIES [6,8]','Use feedback and QoS observations to adjust allocations.','Protected-latency control alone is not a new contribution.'],['Caladan / Shenango [7,9]','Fast core-allocation mechanisms for services.','No comparable microsecond scheduler or deployment evidence.'],['New ARQ probe','A-B-A verification with demand and drift gates.','Synthetic policy evidence only; novelty unresolved.']],[135,187,186])
para('Published systems were not executed in this evaluation. This is a mechanism comparison, not a claim that ARQ outperforms them. The specific conjunction of bracketed measurements and acceptance gates needs a full prior-art and inventive-step review.')
page('Review III: outcome');h('16. Project Outcome and Team Record');para('The deliverable comprises the ARQ source, a local opt-in recovery-verification module, twelve added regression tests, a five-scenario synthetic evaluation, logs and a technical disclosure. It supports a bounded research/prototype outcome rather than a finished production resource manager.')
table(['Person / work area','Record'],[['Rithika.S (24BCE2984)','Team identity taken from supplied Review I. Individual module attribution requires team confirmation.'],['K. Vaishnavi (24BCT0183)','Team identity taken from supplied Review I. Individual module attribution requires team confirmation.'],['New research extension','Code, tests and drafting developed with AI assistance during this chat; human inventorship is not inferred.']],[195,313])
h('17. Conclusion and Future Work');para('ARQ makes process observation and graduated control inspectable. Its original recovery rule has an important limitation: low readings may be caused by the restriction itself. The new opt-in experiment checks a proposed allocation increase with additional measurements and restores the original setting before deciding. Tests establish the implemented behavior on defined inputs; simulation illustrates why demand and stability gates can matter.')
para('Next work is to repair and validate native telemetry, measure actual actuation, add a watchdog and cumulative probing budget, integrate the policy under a shared control lock and run repeated live trials with labelled workloads. Evaluate multicore demand, memory/I/O pressure, application progress and data integrity. Patent review must assess the exact claim combination and the public-disclosure timeline; a patent grant or filing is not claimed.')
